  "answer": "Karen Smith (CFO) has revised the Q2 budget by shifting funds toward emerging market bonds, resulting in a new profit forecast of $9.378 million, which is a 3.5% increase from previous estimates. Rachel Adams (Community Outreach Coordinator) noted that based on this revised profit forecast, $75,000 can be allocated to community initiatives without impacting investment strategies. Diana Wells (Chief Auditor) mentioned that the upcoming Q2 audit will require accurate financial records, particularly those related to these recent budget revisions. Henry Scott (CEO) indicated that Jordan will need to summarize the financial performance, the impact of these budget revisions, and the updated profit forecast during the upcoming Q2 earnings call. Additionally, Emily Rogers (Operations Manager) reported an unplanned IT expenditure of $50,000 that will affect the Q2 budget."
